# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) and fill in. Nothing is required for Milestone 1.
#
# RULE: anything prefixed VITE_ is bundled into the public frontend and visible to
# every visitor. Only PUBLIC values (e.g. a Supabase anon key, which is protected by
# row-level security) may ever use that prefix. Privileged keys (service-role keys,
# API keys for data providers or LLMs) belong ONLY in the content pipeline's
# environment / CI secrets, never in the web app.

# --- Added in a later milestone (hosted backend) ---
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Content pipeline (server/CI side ONLY; never prefix these with VITE_) ---
# Used by `pipeline/` to generate candidate questions. Local: put the real value in `.env`.
# CI: add it as a GitHub Actions secret named OPENAI_API_KEY (Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions).
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# The model name is deliberately not hard-coded; set the one you want to use.
# PRILLION_OPENAI_MODEL=

# --- Added in a later milestone ---
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
